{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he said, 'My son's tunic.'</b> This is it." "<b>A wild beast has devoured him.</b> The holy spirit flickered in him — his end is that Potiphar's wife will ensnare him. And why did the Holy One, blessed be He, not reveal it to him? Because they had banned and cursed anyone who would reveal, and partnered the Holy One, blessed be He, with them (Tanchuma). But Yitzchak knew that he was alive — he said, How can I reveal when the Holy One, blessed be He, does not wish to reveal it to him?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:30.808561100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}